# Theme CSS convention

The storefront and auth pages support a Dark and a Light theme, chosen in Admin > Website.
The layouts render `<html data-theme="dark|light" data-bs-theme="dark|light">` and load `public/css/theme.css`.

## Rules

1. Never hard-code hex/rgb text or background colors in views. Use the tokens from `public/css/theme.css`:
   - Backgrounds: `--fc-body-bg`, `--fc-surface`, `--fc-panel`, `--fc-input-bg`, `--fc-img-bg`, `--fc-nav-bg`, `--fc-dropdown-bg`, `--fc-overlay-bg`
   - Text: `--fc-text`, `--fc-heading`, `--fc-muted`, `--fc-link`, `--fc-link-hover`, `--fc-accent`, `--fc-on-accent`
   - Borders/shadows: `--fc-border`, `--fc-border-soft`, `--fc-border-strong`, `--fc-focus-ring`, `--fc-shadow`
   - Brand gradient: `var(--fc-gold)` to `var(--fc-amber)`
2. When a section needs colors that differ per theme, write both selectors:

```css
[data-theme="dark"]  .my-section { background: #0f1626; color: #f7f1e3; }
[data-theme="light"] .my-section { background: #fff8ec; color: #1f2433; }
```

3. Any new token must be added to both the dark and the light block in `public/css/theme.css`.
4. Avoid dark-only or light-only Bootstrap classes (`table-dark`, `text-dark`, `bg-white`, `text-white`, `bg-dark`). Prefer theme-neutral classes (`table`, `text-body`, `text-secondary`) or tokens.
5. Exceptions: QR codes and similar scannable images keep a white background.
6. Store pages extend `layouts.store`; auth pages use `layouts.guest`. Both already apply the theme, so new pages extending them inherit it automatically.
